# What is ignored here, and why.
#
# The rule this file follows: anything the build can produce again from what is
# in the repository does not belong in the repository, and anything a *different*
# machine cannot use is worse than that -- it is a file that looks like
# configuration and is not.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored, and this is the mistake to avoid repeating: the test
# fixtures. xyzpdf/tests/fixtures/*.pdf are written by tools/make_fixtures.py and
# committed on purpose -- the tests open them by relative path, so a checkout
# without them is a checkout whose tests cannot run at all. Same for
# xyzpdf/packaging/app.ico: it is generated by tools/makeappicon.py, but the
# resource compiler needs it on every build, so it is committed and the script is
# run only when the artwork changes.

# Build directories. build-*/ covers this project's build-local-release, and
# build/ and Build/ are what Qt Creator and Visual Studio make.
build/
Build/
build-*/

# CMake's own output.
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile
install_manifest.txt
compile_commands.json

# Compiled objects, libraries and executables.
*.o
*.obj
*.lo
*.slo
*.a
*.lib
*.la
*.lai
*.d
*.gch
*.pch
*.ilk
*.pdb
*.dll
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.exe
*.out
*.app
*.mod
*.smod
*.dwo

# vcpkg installs into the repository root, next to the sources it builds.
vcpkg_installed/

# Packaging output. The signing certificate in particular: a private key does
# not belong in a repository, even a development one.
#
# Matched without a directory prefix on purpose. Written as
# "xyzpdf/packaging/*.pfx" these would stop ignoring anything the moment the
# program or that folder is renamed -- silently, because a pattern that matches
# nothing is not an error. A pattern with no slash matches at any depth.
**/packaging/*.pfx
**/packaging/*.cer
**/packaging/*.msix
**/packaging/*.appx

# Test output. Anchored: CTest writes a Testing/ directory next to the build,
# and unanchored this also matches a source folder called testing/ -- git
# compares ignore patterns case-insensitively on Windows, so "testing" would be
# swallowed too.
/Testing/
.cache/

# Editor and IDE state. .vscode/settings.json in this repository holds an
# absolute path to one machine's source directory (cmake.sourceDirectory is
# "H:/test/XYZPDF/xyzpdf"), which is exactly the sort of thing that is useless
# in another checkout. Qt Creator's .qtcreator/ is the same, and more of it.
.vscode/
.qtcreator/

# Temporary files.
*.tmp
*.log
*.bak
*.swp
